<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Canton Military Government</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1925 CE · capital Guangzhou</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The rival government that Sun Yat-sen set up in Guangzhou to defend the constitution against Beijing's warlords, the cradle of the Nationalist revolution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1917 Premier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duan-qirui">Duan Qirui</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/beiyang-government">Beiyang government</a> refused to restore the dissolved parliament. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-yat-sen">Sun Yat-sen</a> launched the Constitutional Protection Movement, and members of parliament who had followed him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a> elected him generalissimo of a military government, with support from southern warlords.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government depended on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxi">Guangxi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a> generals, who forced Sun out in 1918 and ruled through a directorate under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cen-chunxuan">Cen Chunxuan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-jiongming">Chen Jiongming</a> brought Sun back in 1920, and in 1921 he became extraordinary president, but Chen turned against him in 1922. Returning in 1923, Sun accepted Soviet aid, admitted Communists to his party and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/whampoa-military-academy">Whampoa Military Academy</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a> in 1924.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Sun died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in March 1925 while negotiating with the northern warlords. In July 1925 the regime was reorganised as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nationalist-government">Nationalist government</a>, which launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-expedition">Northern Expedition</a> the following year and went on to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1917 CE – 1925 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.85%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1925 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Guangzhou</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sun Yat-sen, Cen Chunxuan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Cantonese, Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Guangzhou Military Government, Constitutional Protection Government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1921&amp;focus=canton-military-government" aria-label="Canton Military Government on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7705 1324 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Canton Military Government lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8025 1580L7868 1006M8025 1580L8025 1580"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7868 1006h0M8025 1580h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8025 1580h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8025 1580h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Guangzhou. <a href="/atlas?year=1921&amp;focus=canton-military-government">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
